From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: keep wpa_supplicant off the scheduled scan

With the kernel's CONFIG_BCMDHD_SCHED_SCAN the driver advertises nl80211
scheduled scan. cfg80211 in kernel 3.10 runs one scheduled scan per
radio, and wpa_supplicant starts one of its own when its network is not
found (events.c, scan.c: wpa_supplicant_req_sched_scan). That would take
the slot wificond needs for the framework's PNO (EINPROGRESS) and scan
with the supplicant's own schedule. disable_scan_offload=1 keeps the
supplicant on normal scans, as before; p2p_supplicant_overlay.conf
already sets it, as do the AOSP emulator configs (goldfish, cuttlefish).
---
diff --git a/configs/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf b/configs/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf
index f004553..42bc175 100644
--- a/configs/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf
+++ b/configs/wifi/wpa_supplicant_overlay.conf
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+disable_scan_offload=1
 p2p_disabled=0
 update_config=1
 pmf=1
